    %% CURRENT implementation; sources and guards in transition inventory.
    state "UNVERIFIED id=1" as UNVERIFIED
    state "VERIFIED id=2" as VERIFIED
    state "SUSPENDED id=3" as SUSPENDED
    state "DELETED id=4" as DELETED
    state "NOTHING id=5" as NOTHING
    state "UNVERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP id=6" as UNVERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP
    state "VERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP id=7" as VERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP
    [*] --> UNVERIFIED
    [*] --> UNVERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP
    UNVERIFIED --> VERIFIED: Base ceremony final commit
    UNVERIFIED --> VERIFIED: finalize_registration_binding! with original bounded verified proof
    VERIFIED --> DELETED: owner-locked Base release and Source audit intent
    VERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP --> DELETED: owner-locked Base release and Source audit intent
    SUSPENDED --> DELETED: owner-locked Base release and Source audit intent
    UNVERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP --> VERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP: sign-up contact finalization
    UNVERIFIED --> VERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP: signup Base ceremony final commit
    UNVERIFIED --> SUSPENDED: withdrawal anonymize
    VERIFIED --> SUSPENDED: withdrawal anonymize
    SUSPENDED --> SUSPENDED: withdrawal anonymize
    DELETED --> SUSPENDED: withdrawal anonymize
    NOTHING --> SUSPENDED: withdrawal anonymize
    UNVERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP --> SUSPENDED: withdrawal anonymize
    VERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP --> SUSPENDED: withdrawal anonymize
    UNVERIFIED_WITH_SIGN_UP --> DELETED: SignUpArtifactCleanup dependent retention
    note right of VERIFIED
        Effective binding requires finalized_at and a live owner.
        Partial unique facts enforce one destination per Identity
        and one effective destination owner; pending rows do not occupy it.
        Release is terminal and replacement requires new evidence.
        Base removal requires the owning authenticated Actor context.
        Release and its Source audit intent commit together.
        Settings replacement releases the old binding fact, keeping its status,
        and finalizes the new candidate with both intents in one Source transaction.
        Signup Ticket failure preserves the committed binding and original audit intent.
        Exact bound checkpoint reconciliation rewrites neither fact.
        Database binding checks reject null, empty and whitespace-only digests.
        Forward recognition requires Source intent or completed signup proof.
        Unknown history or effective conflicts abort with row IDs.
        Existing facts, status and OTP counters remain unchanged.
    end note
